{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/494615-celerity-2-any-use","id":494615,"title":"Celerity 2+...any use?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-28T05:08:51-07:00","id":494615,"title":"Celerity 2+...any use?","content":"So I just went through and reread the Celerity power and... why would anyone buy Celerity at higher dots than 1? You have every good power from the get go - 3XP for +1 defense and extra speed once in a while? I don't think that's worth it.<br /> <br /> Am I missing something?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T05:14:41-07:00","id":494634,"title":"","content":"The number of times you can interrupt actions in a given scene is limited to your dots of Celerity (arguably the discipline's coolest power).<br /> <br /> Don't underestimate how much longevity the higher penalty to attacks will give you. It's significant. <br /> <br /> The extra speed is also not trivial. That extra dot of Celerity can be the difference between &quot;You manage to escape!&quot; vs &quot;Everything goes black as the stake shatters your sternum.&quot; This becomes very clear when you're trying to outrun, or trying to catch, someone else who has Celerity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T05:32:40-07:00","id":494646,"title":"","content":"That &quot;little extra speed&quot; adds up. With celerity 5, an <i>average </i>(2 strength, 2 dex) vampire can run 108 yards a turn. That's about <i>70 miles per hour</i>.<br /> <br /> With every relevant stat maxed out they can manage about <i>300</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 04-28-2015, 08:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T05:49:26-07:00","id":494668,"title":"","content":"If I am not mistaking you add your dots of celerity to your defense as well, so it could mean the difference of you getting hit or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T06:00:33-07:00","id":494674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/494615-celerity-2-any-use?p=494646#post494646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That &quot;little extra speed&quot; adds up. With celerity 5, an <i>average </i>(2 strength, 2 dex) vampire can run 108 yards a turn. That's about <i>70 miles per hour</i>.<br /> <br /> With every relevant stat maxed out they can manage about <i>300</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>*Exactly*. Higher levels of Celerity are very useful. I honestly am not sure where the OP was coming from with the question, save from not having understood the mechanics perhaps....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T06:08:29-07:00","id":494677,"title":"","content":"You don't underestimate someone with high Celerity (or even midtiers). The defense bonus alone is huge, with it you can easily exceed the offenders attack pool and that's even before dodging. <br /> I'd go to the other way of saying that if you're getting a dot of Celerity, why wouldn't you be getting more? You get more of the awesome for no additional in-game cost (same Vitae costs for more benefits). More speed, more defense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T07:41:50-07:00","id":494786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The number of times you can interrupt actions in a given scene is limited to your dots of Celerity (arguably the discipline's coolest power). </div> </div> </div>It's also limited by how much Vitae you can spend in a turn, so unless you have BP5, Cel 5 has no use here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If I am not mistaking you add your dots of celerity to your defense as well, so it could mean the difference of you getting hit or not. </div> </div> </div>That's am important part of Celerity, sure, but Athletics is only 2XP per dot, unlike Cel which is 3 (or 4 if out-of-clan)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> *Exactly*. Higher levels of Celerity are very useful. I honestly am not sure where the OP was coming from with the question, save from not having understood the mechanics perhaps.... </div> </div> </div>I'd like to note that I understand the mechanics, but since Vitae is hard to come by, sprinting a street in a single turn for 15XP worth of investment doesn't seem worth it to me (and it seems like the only important thing to a lot of people here)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'd go to the other way of saying that if you're getting a dot of Celerity, why wouldn't you be getting more? </div> </div> </div>...Because it's a lot of XP investment for almost no real gain back? Seriously at some point the difference between 7 or 8 defense is just not worth it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T07:44:38-07:00","id":494788,"title":"","content":"Scene. How many times per <i>scene</i> you can interrupt. Not per <i>turn. </i><br /> <br /> EDIT: Nixed again, none of the active effects of celerity can activate more than once per turn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":689,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","user":"Smarmy Vamp","date":". 04-28-2015, 10:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T07:47:21-07:00","id":494789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Smarmy Vamp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/494615-celerity-2-any-use?p=494788#post494788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Scene. How many times per <i>scene</i> you can interrupt. Not per <i>turn. </i><br /> <br /> Though there is that also.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> THANKS! It's surprising how a single word clears a lot of things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T07:51:01-07:00","id":494790,"title":"","content":"It's usefulness or lack thereof will depend a lot on your game. If you're not going to be fighting other vampires or dangerous things, or running away from said things, then you don't even need Celerity 1. Otherwise the one with the highest Celerity is more likely to win a Clash of Wills when it comes to deciding who acts first, often a point that can determine a battle. There's also the possibility of Devotions to account for.<br /> <br /> As for the cost between Athletics and Celerity, your Athletics is worthless against guns, while your Celerity still acts as Defense.<br /> <br /> It even has utilitarian uses, a vampire in my last game used it to rush through a security system before it could lower the security shutter to a room.<br /> <br /> And Vitae isn't necessarily hard to come by.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-28-2015, 10:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T07:53:52-07:00","id":494794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/494615-celerity-2-any-use?p=494786#post494786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's also limited by how much Vitae you can spend in a turn, so unless you have BP5, Cel 5 has no use here.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Per <i>scene. </i>Points per turn don't matter at all<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/494615-celerity-2-any-use?p=494786#post494786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's am important part of Celerity, sure, but Athletics is only 2XP per dot, unlike Cel which is 3 (or 4 if out-of-clan)<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Which means it's cheaper/the same price as dots wits/dexterity, which are the other half of the standard equation. Max out athletics, <i>then</i> buy celerity if you prefer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/494615-celerity-2-any-use?p=494786#post494786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'd like to note that I understand the mechanics, but since Vitae is hard to come by, sprinting a street in a single turn for 15XP worth of investment doesn't seem worth it to me (and it seems like the only important thing to a lot of people here)</div> </div> </div> </div>Hello, I'm standing waaay over here, unarmed, and unable to reach you in time to - ohwhoopsIjuststabbedyouintheface.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/494615-celerity-2-any-use?p=494786#post494786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> ...Because it's a lot of XP investment for almost no real gain back? Seriously at some point the difference between 7 or 8 defense is just not worth it.</div> </div> </div> </div>You wouldn't be saying that if you were face-to-face with a rampaging werewolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T08:23:41-07:00","id":494849,"title":"","content":"The difference between 7-8 defense means all the world if your opponent is attacking you with 8 dice and a weapon which has a modifier of +2 or +3 or worse (lethal quality to vamps or something).<br /> <br /> And even then? no real gain back? Compare a vamp with Celerity 1 and Celerity 2 and how one is gonna punch the other's face a lot harder (or escape to survival a lot faster).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T08:43:52-07:00","id":494864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/494615-celerity-2-any-use?p=494790#post494790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the cost between Athletics and Celerity, your Athletics is worthless against guns, while your Celerity still acts as Defense.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is probably the biggest benefit, in my opinion. Celerity adds to overall defense, AND applies itself against Firearms, something no other defense available to vampires does (so far as I am aware). Now, sure, vampires only take bashing damage from firearms, but they also only take bashing damage from (almost) everything else. So all other things being equal, guns are still better than swords, since they ignore a vampire's normal defense stat, allowing you to stack up that bashing damage and eventually roll it over to lethal, then finally Final Death the bloodsucker. Guns can also be used where you're relatively safe from a vampire's hand-to-hand attacks, which are usually their most deadly. With Celerity, not only do you get to apply up to five defense against firearms, as mentioned, speed boosting can make that &quot;safe range&quot; nonexistent. Not only can you dodge bullets, you can Quicksilver to the guy shooting at you and take his gun away. And since Celerity is mostly used by Daeva, who ALSO have Vigor, the old &quot;run-and-punch&quot; can get downright TERRIFYING.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T08:58:34-07:00","id":494877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ErikModi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/494615-celerity-2-any-use?p=494864#post494864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And since Celerity is mostly used by Daeva, who ALSO have Vigor, the old &quot;run-and-punch&quot; can get downright TERRIFYING.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, because Mekhet do not buy Celerity with the same frequency :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T08:58:41-07:00","id":494878,"title":"","content":"I think Celerity 2+ is worth it. The Defense is fantastic. often times that 1 or 2 die means the difference of getting hit or not, which could mean life or death... Or when they toss a grenade in your face, you're just not there when it goes off. I love the Quicksilver reference. It's really great for what exactly celerity can do. Going first then constantly interrupting actions for up to 5 turns could sway the fight heavily in your favor. <br /> <br /> I dont particularly think that Vitae is hard to come by unless.... you're like a 6 BP vamp ... but then celerity's usefulness is not your biggest problem. I personally haven't had a problem with telling my story teller that I need to go feed and then he/she refusing and not letting me get vitae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T09:01:08-07:00","id":494881,"title":"","content":"Well, your situation is pretty &quot;standard&quot;. Go ahead and tell that to your ST as you get chased by werewolves (or hunted). Or when you're in a middle of nowhere <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T09:20:46-07:00","id":494929,"title":"","content":"Depends on the middle of no where... If that middle of no where is in the forest... animals. I mean it might be hard to come by for that night or a few nights, but... just eat the werewolf nom nom nom! Turn the hunt back on whoever is hunting you. Granted my 4-5 games have all be inside a city.... where there are Always people... so I can see other scenarios where it's hard to come by but dont over generalize and say it is &quot;ALWAYS&quot; difficult to get.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T09:53:37-07:00","id":494967,"title":"","content":"I think if you're in the position that you need to eat the werewolf, you're going to have trouble eating the werewolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T10:11:35-07:00","id":494984,"title":"","content":"A wolf is never alone young neonate. Even if it was it is unwise to go toe to toe with one on its terms. It will tear you apart piece by piece. Unless you are certain you have the advantage you run... And it may still catch you (great use of the mentioned discipline as said by others).<br /> <br /> Edit: for clarity sake, neonate is used because i imagine a sire telling their child this lesson.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2909,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","user":"Mr.F.I.X.","date":". 04-28-2015, 02:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T10:54:02-07:00","id":495007,"title":"","content":"Annnnnd we go off on a Tangent ^.^ Why would the pack of wolves even Want to kill the vampire with Idol? Dominate the first wolf the shred the second wolf. Vampire with Celerity moves out of the wolf's attacks and fills him full of Silver bullets. Vampire with Nightmare makes the wolf think that the pack of wolves if actually after him instead. a vampire with 5 vigor 5 strength 5 brawl and 5 BP riding the waves of frenzy could be just as terrifying as a wolf. Why does the vampire have to be alone? Where are his ghouls? his clan? his friends? ok ok ok before we get anymore into this and highjack the thread anymore i am going to say that I really depends on the scenario and who plays it out better. I dont think that Wolves will win end of story. over generalization. I think it could go either way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T11:39:09-07:00","id":495052,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't call that guy a &quot;neonate&quot; but whatever. <br /> <br /> Also a werewolf of similar physical potency would need Purity 5, which makes it more likely they're a rahu, which would in turn mean they had access to Killer Instinct and Crimson Spasm.<br /> <br /> ...Good luck, oh fearless werewolf baiter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T22:59:09-07:00","id":495948,"title":"","content":"So, while we're talking about Celerity...<br /> <br /> Is it a valid thing to use the Celerity interrupt to be like &quot;I use Celerity to interrupt. I'll take my movement to behind you. Your attack misses as you slash at empty space. Now I'll take my instant action and attack you.&quot; Basically using the interrupt as essentially and auto-dodge. Is that within the rules? I remember seeing it somewhere early on that was an intended use of Celerity, but reading the actual rules it seems vague... I think &quot;Move around behind you and stab you&quot; is definitely kosher, but it depends a lot on Storyteller ruling whether that would make the original attacker miss or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2007-wade-l","name":"Wade L","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2007_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T23:04:02-07:00","id":495951,"title":"","content":"I would call it an automatic miss, since I don't think people have yet mastered the ability to &quot;lock on&quot; to superspeeding vampires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T23:53:11-07:00","id":496014,"title":"","content":"Seems like it should work. Though I might have the interrupt fail against specific powers if you're not going to ensure you're out of range of the action in question. If someone has a 2e equivalent of the Quicken Sight Devotion, &quot;locking on&quot; to incredibly vast moving vampires and being able to attack them when they try to use their speed to dodge and attack you seems legit to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T00:01:24-07:00","id":496019,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Quicken Sight would be a great counter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T00:41:28-07:00","id":496031,"title":"","content":"This differs slightly from my interpretation, seeing how the discipline clearly states:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> However, the vampire is still limited to one instant action. She cannot use Celerity to make two attacks, or an attack followed by another instant action </div> </div> </div>I read this as an &quot;autododge&quot; is an instant action and an attack is an instant action. Or is really the intended use that you can make an instant action followed by an attack?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/593-gemstone","name":"Gemstone","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T00:53:07-07:00","id":496039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gemstone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/494615-celerity-2-any-use?p=496031#post496031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This differs slightly from my interpretation, seeing how the discipline clearly states:<br /> <br /> I read this as an &quot;autododge&quot; is an instant action and an attack is an instant action. Or is really the intended use that you can make an instant action followed by an attack?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Each turn a vampire has one Movement, and One Instant action. Celerity allows you to do one of them out of your turn order. You use your movement to get behind him, he slashes empty space, you use your instant action to mess him up.<br /> <br /> As for Quicken Sight, I'm not sure if it's such a counter. Do remember, that Celerity is described as more akin to teleportation. You disappear from one place and appear in the next, without it looking like you passed the space behind. Even saying that Quicken Sight does keep you track the vampire (I'd be in favor of this), I still would say that the attack misses, because being able to follow someone with your eyes don't give you the speed to turn around and smack him in time.<br /> After all, Celerity is used after the target states his action, and he must go through with it. But since the Quicken Sight user has celerity, he can probably also do it to change his action.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T01:02:18-07:00","id":496047,"title":"","content":"I agree. Quicken Sight gives you the perception to see the vampire moving out of the way of your attack, but not the reflexes to counteract your own momentum in time. You know you're going to miss, but unless you can match the vampire's speed, you can't do anything about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T01:16:41-07:00","id":496050,"title":"","content":"I definitely think that celerity should allow you to counter an interrupt <i>somehow</i>, but I'm not entirely sure how it would work crunchwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T01:21:56-07:00","id":496051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/494615-celerity-2-any-use?p=496050#post496050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I definitely think that celerity should allow you to counter an interrupt <i>somehow</i>, but I'm not entirely sure how it would work crunchwise.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, the crunch is simple: if two Kindred try to use the interrupt at the same time there's a clash of wills. Whoever prevails get's to do their action first. <br /> <br /> So it probably goes like this.<br /> <br /> Xplayer &quot;I smack you in the face&quot;<br /> Yplayer &quot;I use celerity to run around you and once you smack the air I punch you in your head&quot;<br /> Xplayer &quot;I use celerity to be even faster than you and smack you before you run around me.&quot;<br /> Commence Clash of Wills of Celerity + BP.<br /> If Y wins, he runs around, get's smacked by player X and then smacks him back.<br /> If X wins, he smacks player Y, player Y runs around him and smacks him in the back. <br /> <br /> And then we roll around to the main question of the thread. This fight will be largely influenced by who has more Celerity and can do the interrupt more times. Woe to the one who only has Celerity one of the other has something like 3 or more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T05:35:38-07:00","id":496195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/494615-celerity-2-any-use?p=496039#post496039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Each turn a vampire has one Movement, and One Instant action. Celerity allows you to do one of them out of your turn order. You use your movement to get behind him, he slashes empty space, you use your instant action to mess him up.</div> </div> </div> </div>I figure you can move and take an instant action during your interrupt. That might be a bit of an interpretation, but it seems to jibe with the inspiration behind the power. <br /> <br /> I'm right with you on Quicken Sight, it would let you track them visually, but QS doesn't improve your physical capabilities at all, so I wouldn't let a character use it to physically intervene in a speeding vampire's interrupt. It would let you see where they went, though, where otherwise they might seem to just disappear into thin air. <br /> <br /> I think the best way to handle &quot;countering&quot; (and I don't care for that term, but that's another discussion) Celerity interrupts is another Celerity user and clash of wills, as you suggested.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T05:43:20-07:00","id":496201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Smarmy Vamp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/494615-celerity-2-any-use?p=496195#post496195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I figure you can move and take an instant action during your interrupt. That might be a bit of an interpretation, but it seems to jibe with the inspiration behind the power.</div> </div> </div> </div>I stand corrected. Went back to the book and reread it, yes , it looks like you can both move and do an action.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T12:20:28-07:00","id":496586,"title":"","content":"You aren't forced to do both though, if for some reason you wanted to hold off on your action.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T12:21:22-07:00","id":496589,"title":"","content":"Right, you can just move to run away and not take an action, whatever combo you wish.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T18:25:47-07:00","id":496937,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't say you can do both during your interrupt. You get one action, not your whole turn, during the interrupt.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vampire: The Requiem 2nd Edition pg 131</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interrupt the action of another character with a brief action of<br /> her own. This could be an attack, making it possible to disable an<br /> opponent in mid-action. It may be movement, avoiding harm by<br /> shifting out of reach. Or it could be any other instant action, like<br /> activating a Discipline or dodging.</div> </div> </div> </div>'<b>A</b> brief action', plus the use of 'or,' makes it seem to me that the intention is not to take your full turn with the interrupt. Move or act, not both. This is already the ability to completely nullify an attack for 1 vitae (unless it's a ranged attack and cover isn't in range), so I feel like letting you interrupt with a full turn tips it over from &quot;very potent&quot; to &quot;OP.&quot;<br /> <br /> Of course, typical caveat of it ultimately being up to the ST, but I personally wouldn't allow that in my game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T00:59:38-07:00","id":497211,"title":"","content":"Movement is not considered an Instant action. Celerity states that it doesn't give you a second Instant action, but movement is not an Instant action.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T01:09:46-07:00","id":497217,"title":"","content":"Unless you try to do it twice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T13:24:09-07:00","id":497802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/494615-celerity-2-any-use?p=497211#post497211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Movement is not considered an Instant action. Celerity states that it doesn't give you a second Instant action, but movement is not an Instant action.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/494615-celerity-2-any-use?p=497217#post497217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless you try to do it twice.</div> </div> </div> </div>The question then is - does the Celerity interrupt force you to make movement your action if you do it in the interrupt? Otherwise, presumably you can interrupt, move, opponent's turn, your instant action, and you've only take one instant action.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2007-wade-l","name":"Wade L","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2007_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T13:41:57-07:00","id":497839,"title":"","content":"...<br /> <br /> What? <br /> <br /> There is no &quot;opponent's turn&quot; There is one turn, everyone moves in order. If you interrupt, that's your action for the turn. You can't take another one. Then the turn rolls over and it's your opponent's go again, then if you don't interrupt, it's yours. <br /> <br /> Really in that situation you're probably better off just using the initiative boost instead though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T23:59:06-07:00","id":498450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/494615-celerity-2-any-use?p=497839#post497839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...<br /> <br /> What?<br /> <br /> There is no &quot;opponent's turn&quot; There is one turn, everyone moves in order. If you interrupt, that's your action for the turn. You can't take another one. Then the turn rolls over and it's your opponent's go again, then if you don't interrupt, it's yours.<br /> <br /> Really in that situation you're probably better off just using the initiative boost instead though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Err, if the word &quot;turn&quot; is confusing, maybe use the word &quot;go&quot; instead or something like that.<br /> <br /> Anyway, everyone gets a movement and an action, right?<br /> <br /> So your opponent starts taking his movement and his action. You interrupt.<br /> <br /> Do you get to take both your movement and your action during your interrupt?<br /> <br /> or<br /> <br /> Do you get to take only your movement <i>or </i>your action, and lose the other? (ironically meaning when you use Celerity you can do less during the turn)<br /> <br /> or<br /> <br /> Do you get to take either your movement or your action during your interrupt, and then get whichever you have left later?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2007-wade-l","name":"Wade L","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2007_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T00:42:39-07:00","id":498462,"title":"","content":"I believe you can do both, but can chose to just do one or the other if you want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T02:56:20-07:00","id":498579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wade L</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/494615-celerity-2-any-use?p=498450#post498450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Err, if the word &quot;turn&quot; is confusing, maybe use the word &quot;go&quot; instead or something like that.<br /> <br /> Anyway, everyone gets a movement and an action, right?<br /> <br /> So your opponent starts taking his movement and his action. You interrupt.<br /> <br /> Do you get to take both your movement and your action during your interrupt?<br /> <br /> or<br /> <br /> Do you get to take only your movement <i>or </i>your action, and lose the other? (ironically meaning when you use Celerity you can do less during the turn)<br /> <br /> or<br /> <br /> Do you get to take either your movement or your action during your interrupt, and then get whichever you have left later?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I believe it's fairly obviously one or the other, based on the post I made earlier. Primarily the use of &quot;It may be movement, avoiding harm by shifting out of reach. <b>Or</b> it could be any other instant action.&quot; (quote from page 131)<br /> <br /> There's really no support for this idea that you can do both in the text.<br /> <br /> However, I don't think it's any of the options you provided, due to: &quot;she cannot move further in a single turn than her Speed would allow.&quot; (also a quote from page 131)<br /> <br /> So, I think it is more &quot;you can interrupt with a move action or an instant action, and you cannot take two instant actions or move more than your Speed in a round.&quot; (not a quote, but my answer to your question given the text above) Namely, you could move half your speed with the interrupt, then use the other half of your speed during your actual turn to move back into range for melee.<br /> <br /> If someone would like to quote some text (as I've been doing) as to why you should be able to do both actions, I'm open to the idea that I'm wrong, but as it stands I only see evidence (as opposed to opinions) that you can do one and only one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T05:07:27-07:00","id":498662,"title":"","content":"If there was clear text to quote either way this wouldn't even be a discussion. <br /> <br /> Using the idea of a move action is misleading. There are no move actions, you can just move up to your speed and still take an instant action. The only time movement or speed is covered in the rules it talks about how far you can move in a turn and still act (your speed). The Celerity interrupt just lets you take your action (and movement up to your speed) out of order and the clauses are supposed to close off any loophole of someone taking multiple actions or multiplying their speed without paying for that effect.<br /> <br /> If you have any unused speed or even your action left after your interrupt, you can use them on your normal initiative.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T12:01:18-07:00","id":499207,"title":"","content":"Except I have twice now provided clear text to support one or the other, not both. No one has provided any text contrary to this, and there is no text in the discipline description that provides the slightest hint that you can do both. With evidence for one interpretation provided and no evidence for the other interpretation, I'm really not sure how this is a debate anymore. However, most people seem attached to &quot;both&quot; for some reason or another. I've stated that I'm open to hearing this other reason, but nobody has provided one.<br /> <br /> It's really strange to me how attached people are to this idea while being unable to provide any supporting evidence, let alone any evidence that contradicts the text I have provided. If you're so sure this is the case, surely at least someone has evidence to back their convictions?<br /> <br /> Literally all anyone is doing is saying &quot;you can do both, or only one if you want.&quot; Nobody is providing the slightest support for this position. All I'm asking for is some measure of evidence, like I have provided. You cannot define RAW by saying &quot;this is just how it is, deal with it.&quot; You could argue that's the case with RAI, maybe, but you really aren't in any position to do so unless you are the author.<br /> <br /> Unless someone can provide counter-text, RAW is doing one or the other. It's clearly stated with an &quot;or&quot; not an &quot;and.&quot; I'm not sure how anyone can argue otherwise, and I'm hoping someone will explain to me why they are. If I'm the only one arguing for this interpretation, I must be missing something obvious and supported by the text, so please elaborate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T12:13:24-07:00","id":499242,"title":"","content":"&quot;Or&quot; means one, the other, or both. If the description means &quot;one or the other, but not both&quot; it should say &quot;but not both.&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm comfortable with you describing my take on the power as interpretation or house rule, by the way. It is both the way I read it, and the way I like it to work in play, so I'm going with that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T12:17:57-07:00","id":499245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Smarmy Vamp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/494615-celerity-2-any-use?p=499242#post499242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Or&quot; means one, the other, or both.</div> </div> </div> </div>That really doesn't sound right.<br /> <br /> 'A single point of Vitae heals two points of bashing damage, or one point of lethal damage.'<br /> <br /> 'By spending a point of Vitae, he may add two dice to rolls involving his choice of Strength, Dexterity, or Stamina for the turn.'<br /> <br /> 'A vampire can smell the presence of blood from about ten yards or meters per dot of Blood Potency without rolling.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-01-2015, 03:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T12:24:41-07:00","id":499252,"title":"","content":"To elaborate a bit further, ignoring word semantics: The way a given character's action works in combat is on their initiative result in the order, they are able to take an instant action. At this time they are allowed to move up to their speed and still take an action. <br /> <br /> The interrupt lets you do that out of order, interfering with another character's declared action before it is executed. There is no &quot;move action.&quot; You are simply able to move up to your speed when you take an instant action. You can do this during an interrupt. <br /> <br /> If you can't do it during the interrupt, the clause clearly stating that you are still limited to moving your speed is unnecessary. How else would you move more than your speed unless you tried to move during the interrupt, then again on your normal initiative result?<br /> <br /> Likewise you can take your action normally, and assuming you haven't used all your speed from the turn, you can still use your interrupt later to move up to the remaining speed. <br /> <br /> If you can quote me a passage saying that your interrupt precludes you from acting or moving on your regular initiative result I'd appreciate it. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T12:34:57-07:00","id":499257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/494615-celerity-2-any-use?p=499245#post499245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That really doesn't sound right.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, retracted. Misuse on my part. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T12:54:16-07:00","id":499267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Smarmy Vamp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/494615-celerity-2-any-use?p=499242#post499242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Or&quot; means one, the other, or both.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/494615-celerity-2-any-use?p=499245#post499245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That really doesn't sound right.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I remember seeing some examples of the casual 'or' (the one that Smarmy Vamp quoted) in some sections of the Vampire book (I want to say animalism, but I'm not sure), though I could be wrong on my interpretation.<br /> Since the books switch between the casual and logical (or exclusive) use of 'or' often enough, I figure it's very much up to the Troupe and the Storyteller which is fair by them with regards to an interpretation.<br /> That being said, I allow Celerity interrupts as a instant action and you can move, since that seems reasonable (at least, with the way that my vamp player does it) and allows for some interesting descriptions* of what the other players can see.<br /> <br /> *: Like when one of them blinks, and the gangster running away is suddenly clothes-lined unto the pavement by a semi-pale Indian 20-something year-old male in a french maid outfit... He's the Troupe clown as it were.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>\u201cThe good sleep better, but the bad seem to enjoy the waking hours much more.\u201d</b> -<i>Woody Allen</i> \u200b<br /> <br /> \u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5322-zimthehacker","name":"Zimthehacker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5322_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T12:59:00-07:00","id":499276,"title":"","content":"I go back to the scene from <i>Interview With the Vampire</i> where Louis turns on the light by zipping across the room in the blink of an eye. Moving across the room and hitting the switch is cooler than zipping across the room, then sitting there for a second and <i>then</i> hitting the switch. <br /> <br /> Yes, it's an imperfect analogy as you could argue that flipping a switch isn't an instant action, but I hope it illustrates my point. Besides, what is and isn't an action narratively vs. mechanically is a complete abstraction with a blurry line as it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T17:25:34-07:00","id":499518,"title":"","content":"Celerity 1 is amazing for everyone and neigh mandatory if your campaign is combat heavy.<br /> Celerity 2+ is amazing for some people.<br /> <br /> First, if you are going for Kindred on Super combat, you simply can not be more efficient than purchasing +Blood Potency, at least until its 3 to 5, after you get Celerity 1 and an Oh Shit button. Blood Potency is simply, hands down, the best bang for your buck EXP wise. Beyond that, it depends on what you are trying to accomplish.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T17:52:29-07:00","id":499557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/494615-celerity-2-any-use?p=499518#post499518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Celerity 1 is amazing for everyone and neigh mandatory if your campaign is combat heavy.<br /> Celerity 2+ is amazing for some people.<br /> <br /> First, if you are going for Kindred on Super combat, you simply can not be more efficient than purchasing +Blood Potency, at least until its 3 to 5, after you get Celerity 1 and an Oh Shit button. Blood Potency is simply, hands down, the best bang for your buck EXP wise. Beyond that, it depends on what you are trying to accomplish.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, vampire fights to the death tend to come down to who runs out of Vitae first.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T21:22:10-07:00","id":499774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/494615-celerity-2-any-use?p=494786#post494786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's also limited by how much Vitae you can spend in a turn, so unless you have BP5, Cel 5 has no use here.</div> </div> </div> </div>It won't affect everything, but just having the &quot;Forced March&quot; devotion from Carthians, pg. 197 makes a lot of difference i think.<br /> <br /> <i>Using this Devotion, the vampire can run at the full speed allowed by her Celerity for the entire duration. Each activation of this power lasts a number of hours equal to the vampire\u2019s Resilience. Activating this Devotion costs 1 Vitae for every two dots of Celerity the vampire possesses, rounded up. Activating this Devotion at purchase level costs 1 Vitae, activating the Devotion with Celerity \u2022\u2022\u2022 or \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 costs 2 Vitae and activating costs 3 Vitae with Celerity \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T22:28:31-07:00","id":499827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/494615-celerity-2-any-use?p=499557#post499557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, vampire fights to the death tend to come down to who runs out of Vitae first.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Don't aggree with SoulGambit. While vampire fights to the death tend to come down to who runs out of vitae first, needing to spend less vitae on healing (due to celerity) is probably more advantagious than holding a few points more of vitae. Frenzy does paint this a little differently becoming + 1 dice and some vitae vs -1 dice and some vitae, but Celerity is cheaper and you will completely ignore several attacks from your opponent. <br /> <br /> So I'd say that BP is not a clear winner here as some people make out it be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T07:36:42-07:00","id":500327,"title":"","content":"Frenzy gives +1 to physical rolls per point of Blood Potency, which will likely increase your speed. Plus Blood Potency boosts your Clash of Wills dicepool, so at a certain point providing you have Celerity at all you can beat out someone with higher Celerity.<br /> <br /> The gains of Blood Potency, even aside from Vitae usage and storage, are pretty impressive, I wouldn't underestimate them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-02-2015, 10:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T08:19:05-07:00","id":500387,"title":"","content":"It's to dice pools, not the traits themselves. It would help in a chase but you don't actually get any faster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T08:21:17-07:00","id":500394,"title":"","content":"Where does it say that? All my book says is that the Stamina bonus doesn't increase their Health.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T08:39:39-07:00","id":500442,"title":"","content":"&quot;Add her Blood Potency dots to any Strength, Dexterity, or Stamina rolls or resistances.&quot; <br /> <br /> I think the intent is that it adds to the roll, but not to the base trait. Yes, it only specifically calls out Stamina and Health, but I think that's an oversight. If it was intended to add to the traits wouldn't it say &quot;Add her Blood Potency dots to her Strength, Dexterity, and Stamina scores?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}